---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Parametric CAD from sketch to shop floor" description="Chudware is an OCCT-powered parametric CAD system for mechanical engineers, available in a browser or as a native Windows and Linux desktop application.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Parametric CAD · Browser or native</p>
          <h1>Parametric CAD, from sketch to shop floor.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Chudware is built for mechanical engineers and product teams who want modeling, assemblies, CAM, PLM, simulation, reverse engineering, and an AI copilot in the same workspace.</p>
          <p class="hero-note">Browser seats run in isolated rootless containers and stream to a tab. Native Windows and Linux preview builds are available on request.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/gallery/">See the actual product</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="product-frame">
          <div class="product-viewport">
            <img src="/images/modeling.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware modeling workspace showing a shelled parametric enclosure and its feature tree" />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="product-caption"><span>Real Chudware workspace</span><span>Feature-based model · OCCT 7.9</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <dl class="architecture-strip" aria-label="Chudware architecture at a glance">
        <div><dt>Geometry</dt><dd>OpenCascade / OCCT 7.9</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Browser delivery</dt><dd>Video-streamed workspace</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Isolation</dt><dd>Rootless container per seat</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Native</dt><dd>Windows + Linux</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="capability-index" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" id="capabilities-title">The engineering loop</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Parametric modeling</li>
        <li>Constraint sketching</li>
        <li>Assemblies</li>
        <li>CAM</li>
        <li>Simulation</li>
        <li>Reverse engineering</li>
        <li>PLM</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="architecture">
    <div class="wrap architecture-layout">
      <header class="section-heading architecture-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">The architecture is the product</p>
        <h2>Full CAD in a browser tab, without turning CAD into a web toy.</h2>
        <p class="lede">A browser seat runs server-side in its own isolated rootless container. Chudware streams the workspace as video and sends input back to the application, so the geometry kernel and the full engineering toolchain stay intact.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">Prefer local execution? Native Windows and Linux builds use the same product surface on an engineering workstation.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="stack-diagram" aria-label="Browser delivery architecture">
        <div class="stack-node stack-client"><span>01</span><strong>Browser tab</strong><small>Display + input</small></div>
        <div class="stack-link"><span>Video</span><span>Input</span></div>
        <div class="stack-node"><span>02</span><strong>Isolated seat</strong><small>Rootless container</small></div>
        <div class="stack-link"><span>Model state</span><span>Tool calls</span></div>
        <div class="stack-node stack-core"><span>03</span><strong>Chudware core</strong><small>C++ · Python · TypeScript · OCCT 7.9</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workbench-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One project, not a relay race</p>
        <h2>Keep design intent attached as the work moves downstream.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The feature tree, manufacturing plan, product data, artifacts, and copilot activity live in one engineering environment instead of being handed between disconnected tools.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="workbench">
        <figure class="workbench-image">
          <img src="/images/cam.png" width="1340" height="838" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware manufacturing workspace showing a CAM job, stock, tools, operations, and toolpath simulation" />
          <figcaption>Captured from Chudware's real manufacturing workspace.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <ol class="workflow-list">
          <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Model with intent</h3><p>Constrained sketches and ordered features keep dimensions, references, and revisions explicit.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Carry geometry into production</h3><p>Build CAM operations and inspect simulation alongside the source design.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Trace the product</h3><p>PLM connects project history and artifacts to the engineering work that produced them.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section copilot-section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI that operates the tools</p>
        <h2>The copilot works inside the model, not in a disconnected chat window.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Describe the engineering intent in plain language. The copilot drives Chudware's modeling tools, and the result remains a normal, inspectable model with sketches and features.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/ai-copilot/">Read the copilot guide</a></div>
      </header>
      <ol class="tool-loop" aria-label="Copilot modeling loop">
        <li><span>Intent</span><strong>Describe the part and its constraints</strong></li>
        <li><span>Context</span><strong>Work against the open model</strong></li>
        <li><span>Tools</span><strong>Drive the same modeling operations</strong></li>
        <li><span>Result</span><strong>Inspect sketches, features, and geometry</strong></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section source-section">
    <div class="wrap source-band">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Built as a system</p><h2>Deep software for physical products.</h2></div>
      <p>Chudware is a large C++, Python, and TypeScript codebase built around the OpenCascade geometry kernel, a feature tree, a 2D constraint solver, manufacturing workflows, product data, and isolated streamed sessions.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/changelog/">Read the changelog <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start in the browser</p>
      <h2>Open a full engineering workspace from a tab.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Create an account for browser access, or ask about a native Windows or Linux preview build.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/download/">Native desktop details</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
